name: verse
description: "Verse itself, acted on by a task as the person it runs for would act on it: each verb is a verb of `verse` and of `verse mcp`, made through verse's API. The runner carries the request with its own token, naming the task, and verse admits it as the task's owner, only while the task runs. A task's own questions, which it waits on as a task, are the question system's."
verbs:
- name: ask-create
  description: "Raise an ask as the person the task runs for, as `verse ask` and verse_ask_create do, and go on without waiting: the call answers `raised question <id>: <question>`, and the ask stands after the task ends. The rows of its `on` run as that person when it settles, and a spawn among them reaches no further than the task does, less charter-install, on its runner and with its credential."
  fields:
  - {name: to, form: doc, description: "whom the ask is put to, as a list of names in the grammar a grant uses ([user:dana@example.com]); absent where anyone may answer"}
  - {name: labels, form: doc, description: "the labels the ask carries, an object of names and values"}
  - {name: on, form: doc, description: "the rows of what follows the answer, each `{match, then}`, as verse keeps them. A row matches them as tony does: `on: !not.all.not {then: {answer: null}}` is a raise some row of which answers another ask"}
- name: ask-get
  description: "Read one of the asks of the person the task runs for, by the name it was asked under or its id, as `verse ask <name|id>` and verse_ask_get do: whether it was answered (`status`, and `answer`, `pending` until it settles, or `why` where it settled with no answer), what it asked and of whom, its due, and what its `on` ran."
- name: ask-list
  description: "List the asks of the person the task runs for, as `verse ask` and verse_ask_list do: each with its id, question, who is asked, its due, its `status`, and its `answer`, `pending` until it settles."
- name: data-get
  description: "Read the verse at an address as the person the task runs for, as `verse data` and verse_data do: the document stored there, or with paths the addresses beneath it, chosen by an if pattern and trimmed to what a trim names."
  fields:
  - {name: path, form: path, description: "the address read, at or under its pattern: `[scratch]` is every address under scratch"}
- name: data-put
  description: "Write a value at an address as the person the task runs for, as `verse data <address> --put` and verse_data_put do: merged into what stands there, on create, update or expect only on that condition, with grants for a node it creates. Answers what stands there after the write."
  fields:
  - {name: path, form: path, description: "the address written, at or under its pattern: `[scratch]` is every address under scratch"}
  - {name: value, form: doc, description: "what is written there, as the write carries it"}
- name: data-rm
  description: "Remove what stands at an address as the person the task runs for, an entity or one field of one, as `verse data <address> --rm` and verse_data_rm do."
  fields:
  - {name: path, form: path, description: "the address removed, at or under its pattern: `[scratch]` is every address under scratch"}
- name: charter-get
  description: "Read the charter at a path as the person the task runs for would, as `verse charter` and verse_charter do: an installed charter as its file, with notes saying what the file cannot (a rule held, suspended or in trouble, and the charters under it), a rule or level as it stands, or with paths one kinded path per rule and level."
- name: charter-check
  description: "Ask whether charters would install at an address, as `verse charter --check` and verse_charter_check do: each charter's verdict, and what the install would add, change and take away. Nothing is installed."
- name: charter-install
  description: "Install charters as the person the task runs for, as `verse charter -a` and verse_charter_install do: each a fielded charter at its own `at:` (with `ttl:`, it is removed when that is over), or a bare rule list at an address, applied as one step, with a prune taking what the charters given leave out under the address. Answers what was installed. A spawn among its rules reaches no further than the task does, less this verb, with no looser autonomy and the task's credential where it spends one, on any runner: what the task installs cannot install charters."
  fields:
  - {name: at, form: path, description: "the address the install acts at: with a prune, the prune's; otherwise the deepest address every charter it installs lies at or under (play.issues.issue). Everything it installs is at or under it, so a shape on it bounds where the task installs: an address is at or under its pattern, whose `*` takes any one segment"}
- name: charter-remove
  description: "Remove what stands in the charters as the person the task runs for, as `verse charter -r` and verse_charter_remove do: a whole charter by its address, or one rule, level or schedule of it by its path."
